Reason:
The bug occurs because when the `copy_vma` function fails to create a new virtual memory area (`new_vma`), it jumps to the `out` label without properly unlinking the anonymous virtual memory areas and closing the associated file. This results in memory leaks since the allocated resources are not freed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (new_vma->vm_file)
    fput(new_vma->vm_file);
```
```c
unlink_anon_vmas(new_vma);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that if the creation of `new_vma` fails, the associated file is properly closed using `fput(new_vma->vm_file)` and the anonymous virtual memory areas are unlinked with `unlink_anon_vmas(new_vma)`. This prevents memory leaks by ensuring that all allocated resources are freed when the function exits due to an error.

